+### D-002: Use ISO dates everywhere
+status: locked
+date: 2026-09-09
+owner: hamza
+author: agent
+model: claude-opus-5[1m]
+links: []
+supersedes: none
+
+All dates in the project are written as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.
+The alternative was locale-formatted dates, which sort wrongly and
+read ambiguously across regions (03/04 is two different days).
+ISO is already what the state ledgers use, so this makes the
+existing practice explicit rather than introducing a new convention.
